Keep a subtitle cue that is still on screen when an HLS subtitle playlist starts or seeks.

FFmpeg's HLS demuxer drops every packet of a playlist that starts before the playlist's target
time: after a seek, and when a playlist starts late. A subtitle rendition always starts late, because
the demuxer leaves it out while the stream information is probed, and it then catches up to the
newest packet read. A cue that began before that moment and was still on screen was dropped with the
rest, so a rendition read from the start lost its first line.

For a subtitle packet with a duration, the comparison now uses its last tick instead of its first,
so a cue arrives when it is still showing at the target, and one that has ended stays dropped.
Pictures and sound keep the comparison of their start.

Applied by BuildFFmpegTask before configure, after 0003. Fixes yuroyami/KiteFFmpeg#126.

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
index ab8452e..b129900 100644
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
